# 基础词 Unit27
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2023红宝书考研英语词汇-基础词
# 描述: 基础词Unit27核心词汇

{{injure}}{/ˈɪndʒər/}}v. 伤害；损伤}}{{Three people were injured in the car accident.}}
{{innocent}}{/ˈɪnəsnt/}}adj. 无辜的；天真的}}{{The jury found the defendant innocent of all charges.}}
{{innovation}}{/ˌɪnəˈveɪʃn/}}n. 创新；革新}}{{Innovation is the driving force behind technological progress.}}
{{input}}{/ˈɪnpʊt/}}n. 输入；投入}}{{We need more input from the team before making a decision.}}
{{inquiry}}{/ɪnˈkwaɪəri/}}n. 询问；调查}}{{The police launched an inquiry into the incident.}}
{{insist}}{/ɪnˈsɪst/}}v. 坚持；坚决要求}}{{He insisted on paying for dinner.}}
{{inspect}}{/ɪnˈspekt/}}v. 检查；视察}}{{The building inspector inspected the new construction.}}
{{inspire}}{/ɪnˈspaɪər/}}v. 激发；鼓舞}}{{Her story inspired many young people to pursue their dreams.}}
{{install}}{/ɪnˈstɔːl/}}v. 安装；设置}}{{They installed a new air conditioning system in the office.}}
{{instance}}{/ˈɪnstəns/}}n. 例子；实例}}{{In this instance, the doctor's advice proved correct.}}
{{instead}}{/ɪnˈsted/}}adv. 代替；反而}}{{He decided to walk instead of taking the bus.}}
{{institution}}{/ˌɪnstɪˈtjuːʃn/}}n. 机构；制度}}{{The university is one of the oldest institutions in the country.}}
{{instruct}}{/ɪnˈstrʌkt/}}v. 指导；命令}}{{The teacher instructed the students to open their textbooks.}}
{{instrument}}{/ˈɪnstrəmənt/}}n. 仪器；乐器}}{{She can play several musical instruments.}}
{{insurance}}{/ɪnˈʃʊərəns/}}n. 保险}}{{Health insurance covers most of the medical expenses.}}
{{intellectual}}{/ˌɪntəˈlektʃuəl/}}adj. 智力的；n. 知识分子}}{{Intellectual property rights are protected by law.}}
{{intelligence}}{/ɪnˈtelɪdʒəns/}}n. 智力；情报}}{{Artificial intelligence is transforming many industries.}}
{{intend}}{/ɪnˈtend/}}v. 打算；想要}}{{I intend to finish the report by Friday.}}
{{intense}}{/ɪnˈtens/}}adj. 强烈的；紧张的}}{{The intense competition made the比赛very exciting.}}
{{intention}}{/ɪnˈtenʃn/}}n. 意图；目的}}{{He had no intention of leaving the company.}}
{{interest}}{/ˈɪntrəst/}}n. 兴趣；利益；利息}}{{She has a strong interest in environmental science.}}
{{interfere}}{/ˌɪntəˈfɪər/}}v. 干涉；妨碍}}{{Please do not interfere with the investigation.}}
{{internal}}{/ɪnˈtɜːrnl/}}adj. 内部的；国内的}}{{The company resolved its internal problems quickly.}}
{{international}}{/ˌɪntərˈnæʃnəl/}}adj. 国际的}}{{The international conference attracted delegates from 60 countries.}}
{{interpret}}{/ɪnˈtɜːrprɪt/}}v. 解释；口译}}{{The guide interpreted the ancient text for the visitors.}}
{{interrupt}}{/ˌɪntəˈrʌpt/}}v. 打断；中断}}{{It is rude to interrupt someone while they are speaking.}}
{{interval}}{/ˈɪntərvl/}}n. 间隔；幕间休息}}{{The buses run at ten-minute intervals during rush hour.}}
{{interview}}{/ˈɪntərvjuː/}}n./v. 面试；采访}}{{She has a job interview at a major corporation tomorrow.}}
{{introduce}}{/ˌɪntrəˈdjuːs/}}v. 介绍；引进}}{{The company introduced a new product line this year.}}
{{invade}}{/ɪnˈveɪd/}}v. 入侵；侵犯}}{{The army invaded the neighboring country at dawn.}}
{{invest}}{/ɪnˈvest/}}v. 投资}}{{She invested a large sum of money in the stock market.}}
{{investigate}}{/ɪnˈvestɪɡeɪt/}}v. 调查；研究}}{{The police are investigating the cause of the fire.}}
{{investment}}{/ɪnˈvestmənt/}}n. 投资}}{{Real estate is a popular long-term investment.}}
{{invite}}{/ɪnˈvaɪt/}}v. 邀请；n. 请柬}}{{She invited all her friends to the birthday party.}}
{{involve}}{/ɪnˈvɒlv/}}v. 涉及；使参与}}{{The project involves many different departments.}}
{{iron}}{/ˈaɪərn/}}n. 铁；熨斗；v. 熨}}{{She ironed her shirt before the meeting.}}
{{island}}{/ˈaɪlənd/}}n. 岛屿}}{{The island is famous for its beautiful beaches and clear water.}}
{{isolate}}{/ˈaɪsəleɪt/}}v. 隔离；孤立}}{{The patient was isolated to prevent the spread of infection.}}
{{issue}}{/ˈɪʃuː/}}n. 问题；期；v. 发行}}{{Climate change is one of the most pressing issues of our time.}}
{{item}}{/ˈaɪtəm/}}n. 项目；条款；物品}}{{Each item on the agenda was discussed in detail.}}
